## Findings
- Dashboard:
    - `CUSTOMISE` / `MANAGE` buttons: 10px
    - Stats labels (`TASKS`, `CLASSES`, etc.): 10px
    - Command Center timestamps: 10px
    - `TODAY` label in Agenda: 10px
    - Agenda course titles: 11px
    - Agenda course codes: 9px
- Course Page:
    - Stats labels (`ACTIVE MODULES`, etc.): 10px
    - Semester info: 10px
    - Credits/Exam info: 10px
    - Bottom action buttons (`Tasks`, `Notes`, `Unpin`): 12px (text-xs)
- General Observation:
    - Extensive use of `text-[10px]` and `text-[9px]` classes across all main pages.
    - Important metadata (times, locations, class titles) is often 10px, which is too small for readability.
    - Primary action buttons (Customise, Manage) are 10px.
    - Primary text in cards (Course titles in Timetable/Agenda) is often 10px or 11px.
